<title>ITALY: Bank bad loans rise 15.8 pct in July-Bank of Italy.</title>
<headline>Bank bad loans rise 15.8 pct in July-Bank of Italy.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bad loans at Italian banks rose 15.8 percent in July from a year earlier, slightly above the 15.4 percent annual increase in June.</p>
<p>According to data given in a supplement to the Bank of Italy's statistical bulletin, bank bad loans were 116,764 billion lire in July, up from 100,819 billion lire in July 1995 and compared with 115,421 billion in June 1996.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129502</p>
